# Squash commit (extended description)

When writing the **squash-merge commit message** (the permanent message on `main` after squash), or when asked for an "extended description" / "commit description" for merge:

1. **Read and follow** `.context/commit-description-generator.md` in full.
2. Analyze the **full** branch vs merge base, not only the latest commit.
3. Match recent **merge** commits on the base branch for tone and structure.
4. Output only the message inside one fenced code block (72-char hard-wrapped body, Conventional Commits subject ≤ 50 chars), as that file requires.

This is not the GitHub PR body. For PR titles/bodies, use the pr-descriptions rule and `.context/pr-description-generator.md`.

No AI attribution in the commit message.
